  "finding": "An axisymmetric field is purely axial on the axis, so plasma moving along the axis forward is not reflected (T03 has no stopping radius at polar 0). Anything inside that channel (shield face centre, snout tip, shutter) receives the raw pulse: about 350 J/cm2 of MeV/u ions per pulse. No solid survives this; it needs an axis plug (a sacrificial or renewable stagnation target, or a non-axisymmetric field), and the 0.23-0.32 % of plasma it stops must be booked as hardware heat (FDP-1 already books it in plume_to_hardware)."
